cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this manuscript or verification code, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "A recursive Buchstab switching improvement for the greatest prime factor of n^2+1"
abstract: >-
  Verification code and manuscript for a greatest-prime-factor weak form of
  Landau's fourth problem. The claimed theorem is P+(n^2+1) > n^1.323 for
  infinitely many positive integers n, subject to the Grimmelt--Merikoski
  Type I/II estimates, the standard dimension-one linear sieve, and the
  finite Mellin--Perron transfer recorded in the paper. An outward-rounded
  integer certificate, recomputed in Lean 4, C++, and Python, proves a
  recursive Buchstab-tail saving of at least 0.032303187971.
